<details class="news-item"><summary><time>Sep 2024</time><span>TEACHING</span><strong>Teaching in Autumn 2024</strong><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div><p>During T1 of the 2024/25 academic year, I am teaching Numbers, Sequences and Series and Differential Geometry at the University of Hull.</p></div></details>
</div></section>
<section class="home-section home-background-section"><div class="home-background-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Background</p><h2>A research career across the UK and Austria</h2><p>My approach was shaped by an EPSRC-funded PhD at the University of Sussex, postdoctoral research in motion-aware medical imaging at the University of Graz, and faculty roles in Austria and the UK.</p><p>At the University of Hull I held a permanent Lecturer in Applied Mathematics post—the UK academic grade closest to Assistant Professor—and served as Programme Director for the MSc in Mathematics. That career also developed my skills in leadership, collaboration, supervision, technical documentation and communication.</p></div><a class="section-link" href="https://www.silviofanzon.com/about.html">About my background →</a></section>
</main>
